.TH MEDIAPLAYER 1 "October 2026" "LikeOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mediaplayer \- play music, videos and internet streams
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mediaplayer
.RB [ \-\-fullscreen ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-video ]
.RB [ \-\-shuffle ]
.RB [ \-\-repeat =\c
.IR mode ]
.RB [ \-\-video\-sink =\c
.IR name ]
.RI [ file | folder | playlist | URL ...]
.br
.B mediaplayer \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mediaplayer
is the desktop's music and video player, the program behind
.B Media Player
in the Programs menu and the one a double-clicked song or film opens in.
It plays whatever the installed GStreamer plug-ins can decode: WAV, AIFF and
AU sound, AAC and M4A, MP4, Matroska and WebM video with H.264, H.265, VP8 and
VP9 pictures, and MP3, Vorbis, Opus and FLAC where the FFmpeg decoders are
enabled.  Streams play from
.BR http ,
.B https
and every other kind of address a GStreamer source element is installed for,
including HLS and DASH.
.PP
The window shows the picture (or, for music, the album cover) with a control
bar below it, and the play queue at the right.  Sound goes through
.BR autoaudiosink ,
which picks the system's sound service, so the player mixes with everything
else that is making a sound.
.PP
Each file, folder, playlist or address given on the command line is added to
the queue, and the first one starts playing.  Folders are searched
recursively for media files, which are queued in name order (\(lqTrack 2\(rq
before \(lqTrack 10\(rq), each folder's files before its sub-folders.
Hidden files and folders are skipped.  M3U, M3U8 and PLS playlists are read
and their entries queued; relative entries are taken relative to the
playlist, and Windows-style backslash paths are understood.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-fullscreen
Start in full screen.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-no\-video
Play the sound only.  Video streams are not decoded at all, which saves the
processor time a film's pictures would cost; the cover-art page is shown
instead.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-shuffle
Turn shuffle on.  Like the button, this is remembered for the next start.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-repeat =\c
.I mode
Set the repeat mode:
.B none
(or
.BR off ),
.B all
(start the queue over at its end) or
.B one
(play the current entry again and again).  Remembered like the button.
.TP
.BR \-\-video\-sink =\c
.I name
Choose how pictures reach the screen, for this run only:
.RS
.TP 8
.B auto
The default: the first of
.BR xv ,
.B gtk
and
.B x11
that works.
.TP
.B xv
The X video extension.  The X server (and the graphics hardware behind it)
converts and scales the picture, which makes it the cheapest by far.  Needs
an Xv adaptor;
.BR xvinfo (1)
lists them.
.TP
.B gtk
Pictures drawn by GTK.  Works on every display, but scales in software.
.TP
.B x11
Plain X images.  Cannot scale, so the picture is shown at its own size.
.TP
.B gl
GTK's OpenGL area.  Never chosen automatically.
.RE
.IP
If the chosen output cannot be opened, the automatic order is tried.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the program's and GStreamer's versions and exit.
.PP
The standard GTK and GStreamer options are accepted as well
.RB ( \-\-display ,
.BR \-\-gst\-debug\-level ,
and so on); see
.BR "mediaplayer \-\-help\-all" .
.SH THE WINDOW
.TP
.B Seek bar
Drag it, click it, or scroll on it.  While it is dragged the picture follows
in key-frame steps; the final position is reached exactly when it is let go.
Clicking the time at its right switches between the length of the entry and
the time remaining.
.TP
.B Transport
Shuffle, previous, play/pause, next, repeat and stop.  Previous restarts the
current entry when more than three seconds of it have played, and goes to the
entry before otherwise.  The repeat button cycles through off, all and
\(lqthis one\(rq.
.TP
.B Volume
The slider follows the way loudness is heard (a cubic scale), so its middle
sounds like half.  It controls this program's stream only; the system volume
is
.BR audioctl (1).
Turning the volume up also unmutes.
.TP
.B Play queue
Double-click an entry, or select it and press Enter, to play it.  Entries are
reordered by dragging them, or with the arrow buttons below the list; Delete
removes the selected ones.  Files and folders dropped on the list are inserted
where they fall; dropped on the picture they are added and played at once.
Titles, artists and lengths of queued local files are read in the background
before they play.  The right mouse button opens a menu with the same actions.
.TP
.B Menu
Open files, folders, locations and playlists; save the queue as a playlist;
choose the audio track and the subtitles of a film with several; set the
playback speed (the pitch is kept); show the media information window, the
keyboard shortcuts and the version.
.TP
.B Full screen
Double-click the picture, press
.B F
or F11, or use the button.  The control bar slides away while the pointer
rests and comes back when it moves; Esc leaves full screen.
.PP
The middle mouse button on the picture plays or pauses, the right one opens
the menu, and the scroll wheel changes the volume.
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP 22
.B Space
Play or pause.
.TP
.B N\fR,\fP P
Next or previous entry (also Ctrl+Right and Ctrl+Left, and the media keys).
.TP
.B Left\fR,\fP Right
Back or forward 5 seconds; with Shift, one minute.
.TP
.B Home
Back to the beginning.
.TP
.B 0 \fR...\fP 9
Jump to 0 %, 10 % ... 90 % of the entry.
.TP
.B Up\fR,\fP Down
Volume up or down by 5 %; also + and \-.
.TP
.B M
Mute or unmute.
.TP
.B S
Shuffle on or off.
.TP
.B R
Repeat: off, all, this one.
.TP
.B [\fR,\fP ]
Slower or faster (0.5\(mu to 2\(mu); Backspace returns to normal speed.
.TP
.B F\fR,\fP F11
Full screen on or off.
.TP
.B Esc
Leave full screen.
.TP
.B T
Show the length or the time remaining.
.TP
.B I\fR,\fP Ctrl+I
Media information: tags, codecs, picture size, sample rate, and which video
and sound outputs are in use.
.TP
.B F9
Show or hide the play queue.
.TP
.B Delete
Remove the selected queue entries (while the queue has the keyboard).
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Open files; Ctrl+Shift+O opens a folder.
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
Open a location (an internet address).
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Save the queue as a playlist.
.TP
.B F1
The list of shortcuts.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit.
.PP
While the queue has the keyboard (after it is clicked), the arrow keys move
through it; clicking the picture gives them back to seeking and the volume.
.SH ERRORS
An entry that cannot be played is marked in the queue and explained in a
dialog, with the technical details folded away beneath.  When GStreamer
reports that it needs a plug-in that is not installed, the dialog names it
\(em \(lqMPEG-1 Layer 3 (MP3) decoder\(rq, for example.  A film whose
pictures play but whose sound (or subtitles) cannot be decoded keeps playing,
with a note above the picture.
.PP
When the queue moves on by itself and the next entry fails, that entry is
skipped with a note instead of stopping everything behind a dialog, unless
every entry in turn has failed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mediaplayer/settings
What is remembered between runs: volume and mute, shuffle and repeat, the
window and queue sizes, whether the queue is shown, the folder the file
chooser last opened, and the keys below.  A key file with one
.B [Player]
group, written with mode 0600.  Keys that are missing, mistyped or out of
range fall back to their defaults one by one.
.RS
.TP 20
.B video-sink
The default for
.BR \-\-video\-sink .
.TP
.B gapless
.B true
(the default) to run consecutive entries together without a pause.
.TP
.B discover-metadata
.B false
to stop titles and lengths of queued files from being read ahead.
.TP
.B subtitles
.B false
to start with subtitles hidden.
.RE
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/mediaplayer.desktop
The desktop entry: the applications menu, and the file manager's \(lqOpen
With\(rq list.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MEDIAPLAYER_VIDEO_SINK
Used instead of the remembered
.B video-sink
when no
.B \-\-video\-sink
is given.
.TP
.B GST_DEBUG
GStreamer's own diagnostics, as for every GStreamer program.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The window was closed.
.TP
.B 1
The display could not be opened, or GStreamer (or its
.B playbin
element) is missing.
.TP
.B 2
A bad option.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR audioplay (1),
.BR audioctl (1),
.BR eventsound (1),
.BR xvinfo (1)
